## Enforcement Model

Silver Bullet's quality enforcement happens through three layers in Forge:

1. **Skills (auto-applied)** — at `~/forge/skills/` and `.forge/skills/`. Forge picks the right skill based on context. ~109 skills + ~50 commands loaded — silver-feature, silver-bugfix, silver-ui, silver-devops, silver-release, silver-spec, silver-ensure-docs, silver-handoff, silver-quality-gates, silver-blast-radius, all review-* skills, Anthropic engineering/design/product-management/marketing skills, Superpowers skills, etc.

2. **Hook-equivalent agents (you invoke as tools)** — at `~/forge/agents/` and `.forge/agents/`. These replace the automatic firing of SB hooks on Claude Desktop. You **must** invoke them as tools at the gating moments listed below.

3. **GSD subagents (you invoke as tools)** — at `~/forge/agents/`. These replace `Task(subagent_type=…)` from Claude Code with proper Forge custom-agent delegation. ~33 GSD subagents available + Superpowers code-reviewer.

