## Multi-Agent Coordination (v0.29.0+)

When `.planning/.phase-locks.json` is present, this Forge instance participates in cooperative phase ownership across SB-bearing coding agents. The invariant is **one phase = one runtime at a time**.

### At session start

`forge-session-init` peeks `.planning/.phase-locks.json` and surfaces any non-`forge` locks under "Active phase locks (other runtimes)" in the session summary. Surface this to the user — it tells them which phases are in flight elsewhere.

### Phase boundaries

The silver-* parent skills (`silver-feature`, `silver-bugfix`, `silver-ui`, `silver-devops`, `silver-release`, `silver-spec`) invoke three custom agents at deterministic boundaries:

- **Phase entry:** `forge-claim-phase <NNN>|<intent>` — on `BLOCKED:`, stop and surface to user.
- **During long-running work:** `forge-heartbeat-phase <NNN>` — every wave / verify pass / >5 min op.
- **Phase exit:** `forge-release-phase <NNN>` — after `gsd-ship` for the phase.

### Delegation (`/forge-delegate`)

When this Forge instance holds a lock and wants to delegate work to a sibling runtime, invoke `/forge-delegate` (with optional `--target=claude|codex|opencode|forge`). The child runs with `SB_PHASE_LOCK_INHERITED=true` so it does not double-claim. The structured result (`## FILES_CHANGED` / `## ASSUMPTIONS` / `## REQ-IDS`) is parsed back and integrated into the parent phase's working SUMMARY. The lock stays with this Forge instance throughout.

See `docs/multi-agent-coordination.md` for the full diagram.
